&lt;p&gt;JetBrains is a well-known international software development company. Ever since we started, back in 2000, we’ve strived to make the strongest, most effective developer tools on earth. Our products are trusted by more than 15 million users worldwide, and 88 Fortune Global 100 companies are our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we’re best known in the developer community, JetBrains is home to over 2,500 internationally minded professionals working in offices across Europe, the US, the Middle East, and Asia. If you’re passionate about doing meaningful work, making a tangible impact, and embracing a collaborative culture that favors continuous improvement, you’ll find your place here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced Finance Business Partner with a global mindset to join our FP&amp;amp;A team. In this role, you will act as a trusted advisor to business leaders, supporting strategic decision-making through insightful analysis, financial planning, and performance management. You will work closely with stakeholders from various departments to ensure that financial insights translate into actionable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you thrive in a dynamic environment, welcome change, and enjoy combining analytical depth with business acumen, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a 2-year fixed-term maternity cover position.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business stakeholders to bring a financial perspective to product and investment decisions;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead budgeting, forecasting, and reforecasting processes for your area, ensuring that assumptions are validated, plans are realistic, and resource allocations reflect business and company priorities;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze key financial and operational metrics to identify trends, risks, and opportunities and provide actionable recommendations to business leaders;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear and insightful reports and presentations for senior management, explaining financial performance and key business drivers;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad-hoc business cases for new initiatives, estimating costs, returns, and financial impact together with business stakeholders;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the FP&amp;amp;A, Controlling, and Data teams to maintain consistency, accuracy, and transparency in reporting and financial data;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve planning models, reporting tools, and analytical processes to enhance forecasting quality and decision making;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster financial literacy and accountability across the organization by helping non-financial stakeholders understand the numbers behind their decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be successful in this role if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Finance Business Partner, Financial Analyst, or similar FP&amp;amp;A role in a multinational or fast-growing company;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of financial planning, budgeting, and performance management processes;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate data into insights that drive business action;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency in Excel and experience with FP&amp;amp;A tools and BI platforms (e.g., Tableau, Power BI, BOARD, or similar);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and the ability to engage confidently with technical and product stakeholders;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills, especially when simplifying complex financial topics for non-financial audiences;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive mindset, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At JetBrains, we believe great software is built by great people – and great decisions are powered by great data. As a Finance Business Partner, you’ll have the opportunity to shape the way we plan, analyze, and steer our business. You’ll collaborate closely with leaders across departments, combining analytical depth with strategic thinking to ensure our financial foundation supports innovation and excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us to shape how financial insights guide the future of JetBrains.&lt;/p&gt;
