&lt;p&gt;As Head of JS/TS Ecosystem, you will own the mid- and long-term strategy for JetBrains products for JavaScript and TypeScript developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role focuses on aligning product direction, go-to-market efforts, and external partnerships with the rapidly evolving web development ecosystem. You will translate ecosystem signals – from frameworks and tooling to community practices – into clear strategic priorities for JetBrains products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with engineering, product management, marketing, and developer advocacy teams, and represent JetBrains in the broader web developer community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the strategy and direction for JetBrains products for web developers. Start new product directions when important niches are not addressed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the work for product management, marketing, developer advocacy, and partnerships in the web ecosystem, and keep everyone working toward one plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track important changes and trends in the web community (frameworks, tooling, major releases, new workflows).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with key people in the web ecosystem (companies, open-source projects, community leaders).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering and QA leads to set priorities and plan work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent JetBrains in the web ecosystem at key events and meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with other ecosystems when areas overlap (e.g. Databases, Go, AI).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of how web developers work: JavaScript/TypeScript, major frameworks (especially React), Node.js and browser tooling, package managers, build tools, code quality tools (linting/formatting), testing, and performance tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting product direction based on market needs as a Product Manager or Head of Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading work across product management, marketing, developer advocacy, and business development, directly or through cross-team leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong external-facing capability, including partnerships, community engagement, and executive-level communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to use data for decisions, combining community feedback with product usage and business results.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join JetBrains?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong base salary. We offer competitive pay that reflects your skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work location. Enjoy the freedom to work from home or from the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote work. Spend up to 30 days per year working remotely from abroad.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra time off. More days to relax, recharge, and do the things you love.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical insurance allowance. Enjoy peace of mind for you and your family.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities. Access to conferences, courses, and language classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language classes. Pick up the local language or sharpen your English skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fuel your day. Enjoy a hot meal or receive a lunch allowance on workdays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health support. To help you feel your best, we provide easy access to professional mental health services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sports benefit. Enjoy an on-site gym or sports club stipend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal events. Join company-wide celebrations and team gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation support. We help make your move as smooth and stress-free as possible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;*Some benefits may vary depending on location.
